{
 "_doc": "SGEA-authored: how to evaluate AWS Config conformance-pack rules against a Terraform PLAN (preventive), for the resource types SGEA emits. The rules themselves (and their parameters) are AWS's, from catalog/<baseline>.json; only this rule->plan-attribute mapping is SGEA's. Validated against sources/provider-schema/ by tools/build_catalog.py. `sgea check` evaluates every mapped rule that a composed baseline's pack contains; rules whose resource type is not in the plan are N/A (Config still evaluates them at runtime). `subject`: the resource type the rule is about (default: `resource`); when the subject is absent the rule is N/A, when it is present but `resource` is missing the rule FAILS. `link`: [resource_attr, subject_attr] evaluates per subject instance; `exempt`: {tag: [values]} skips subject instances carrying that tag (reported). ops: equals | not_equals | one_of | set | min | max | contains | count_min | exists. value_param: take the target from the rule's pack parameter; value_from: from the resolved config. `cfn_rules`: the same rules expressed against a synthesized CloudFormation template (CDK output), evaluated by `sgea check --cfn`; `__ref__` links to a resource's logical id via {Ref}. `config_evidence`: when the planned value is only known after apply, PASS if EVERY call of `module_source` in the plan configuration sets `input` to the constant `equals` (the module's documented behavior).",
